overlay-root (4.0.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Modified 2026 by m4dm4x1337 (fixed legacy overlayfs support, see
    v4.0.0 changelog)
    - Replace the static modules.d entry with a hook that selects the
      correct overlay module for each kernel version
    - Detect kernels with overlayfs built in
    - Install the init-bottom script under /usr/share/initramfs-tools
    - Support both overlay and the legacy overlayfs driver
    - Skip workdir when using the legacy overlayfs driver
    - Remove aufs support and the root-ro-driver kernel parameter because
      aufs keeps direct references to its branch mounts, preventing systemd
      from cleanly unmounting them during shutdown; aufs is also out-of-tree
      and no longer available in current distributions
    - Create the upperdir after mounting tmpfs on the writable layer
    - Add the optional root-ro=volatile mode for Linux 5.10 and newer
    - Renumber error messages consistently
    - Correct inherited spelling, grammar, and documentation errors in the
      init-bottom script
  * Avoid rebuilding the initramfs a second time when the package is purged.
  * Remove the obsolete init-bottom conffile when upgrading from version 3.

 -- m4dm4x1337 <madmax@example.invalid>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:34:03 +0100

overlay-root (3.0.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Modified 2023 by m4dm4x1337 (fixed 2 bugs, see v3.0.0 changelog)
    - Resolve root fs symlink if any (e.g. /dev/mapper/ link if root
      is encrypted)
    - Taking tabs into account in /etc/fstab

